      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::001::introduction::7b08936e5e"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The segregated surface layer acts as a diffusion barrier.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::001::introduction::7b08936e5e"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The surface barrier preserves the nanoparticle core's solid-solution structure during catalytic and thermoelectric service.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::001::introduction::7b08936e5e",
        "PMC7229066::chunk::001::introduction::80504fe1f3"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting near-equiatomic nanoparticles have a homogeneous solid-solution alloy structure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::chunk::001::introduction::889f2a282a",
        "PMC7229066::chunk::001::introduction::80504fe1f3"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled annealing can purposefully generate a selectively segregated oxide or intermetallic surface layer.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::001::introduction::7b08936e5e"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The selectively segregated layer limits further elemental diffusion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::001::introduction::7b08936e5e"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting elemental diffusion prevents deleterious restructuring of the nanoparticle core.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Specific annealing conditions favor selective elemental segregation at nanoparticle surfaces.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Selective surface segregation forms a kinetically stabilized surface compound.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The surface compound is self-healing and protects against further oxidation.",
